# =============================================================================
# .env.functions — build-time config for the Cloud Functions DEPLOY
# =============================================================================
# Copy to `.env.functions` (repo root, gitignored) and fill in per environment.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Firebase evaluates function options during "codebase
# analysis", before any env exists, so every `build.mjs` inlines these with an
# esbuild `define` read from `process.env`. That made `export`-in-the-deploy-shell
# the only supply route, and forgetting the export is exactly what the deploy
# preflight now refuses (#1133/#1148). This file is the ergonomic alternative.
#
# ⚠️ IT CAN ONLY DELIVER WHAT A `build.mjs` INLINES. The predeploy hooks that read
# this file are CHILDREN of `firebase deploy`; firebase-tools' trigger-analysis
# process is their SIBLING and inherits the deploy shell, not them. So a name that
# is not `define`d into the bundle cannot travel this way, and the loader refuses
# it rather than pretending. Two families are refused with instructions:
#
#   MERCADO_LIVRE_STOCK_DISPATCHES_PER_SECOND / _CONCURRENT_DISPATCHES
#     `rateLimits`, read by trigger analysis → `export` in the deploy shell.
#   NFE_TASKS_REGION / MERCADO_PAGO_TASKS_REGION / WHATSAPP_TASKS_REGION /
#   BALANCO_TASKS_REGION
#     read at RUNTIME inside the function → that codebase's `.env.deploy`.
#
# ⚠️ THE REAL SHELL STILL WINS. A value already exported is left alone, so CI
# (which exports these directly) is unaffected and a one-off
# `FUNCTIONS_REGION=… firebase deploy` still overrides the file.
#
# ⚠️ WHY NOT `.env.local`. The deploy artifact is uploaded to the project's
# `gcf-sources-*` bucket AND baked in plaintext into the Cloud Run revision, so
# anything the build reads is shipped. `.env.local` holds credentials, which is
# why no `build.mjs` has ever loaded it. This file is safe from that because it
# sits at the REPO ROOT: `copyDeployEnv` only ever scans the functions PACKAGE
# directory, so a root file is never copied into an artifact.
#
# ⚠️ NEVER put a secret here. Not a client secret, not an HMAC key, not a cert
# password — those belong in Secret Manager, and nothing the build reads. The
# allow-list (`BUILD_ENV_KEYS` in `tools/deploy-env/build-env.mjs`) refuses them.
#
# ⚠️ Per WORKTREE. "Repo root" means this checkout's root, so a git worktree needs
# its own copy — same trap `.env.local` documents.
#
# Check what a deploy would use, without deploying:
#   node tools/deploy-env/preflight.mjs mercado-livre
# =============================================================================

# --- Cloud Tasks invoker (ALL FIVE functions codebases, #1133) ---------------
# Comma-separated service-account EMAILS allowed to enqueue AND dispatch this
# repo's task functions. Applied as `invoker` on every `onTaskDispatched`, which
# makes the deploy grant roles/run.invoker on each Cloud Run service (the DISPATCH
# leg, whose absence writes NO failure document anywhere) and
# roles/cloudtasks.enqueuer on each queue.
#
# ⚠️ AUTHORITATIVE: a deploy REPLACES the members of both bindings, so name every
# enqueuer or the one you omit loses the role:
#   - the App Hosting runtime SA — the receiver routes
#     (firebase-app-hosting-compute@<project>.iam.gserviceaccount.com)
#   - the functions runtime SA — the sweeps, the Firestore triggers and every
#     self-continuation (<project-number>-compute@developer.gserviceaccount.com)
# Drop the duplicate when the two are the same identity. Find them with:
#   firebase apphosting:backends:get <backend> --project <id> --json
#   firebase functions:list --project <id> --json     (field: serviceAccount)
TASKS_INVOKER_SA=

# --- Regions ----------------------------------------------------------------
# ⚠️ ONE NAME, TWO MEANINGS, and this file is PERSISTENT. `FUNCTIONS_REGION`'s
# build.mjs default differs per codebase: us-east1 for `storage` and `nfe`,
# us-east5 for `mercado-livre`, `mercado-pago` and `whatsapp`. A value set here
# applies to whichever codebase you deploy next — including ones whose default it
# silently overrides. Prefer exporting it per deploy; set it here only once every
# codebase you deploy from this checkout agrees on one region.
#
# ⚠️ Cloud Tasks and Cloud Scheduler DO NOT EXIST in us-east5. For mercado-pago
# and whatsapp the task functions inherit this value, so their us-east5 default
# makes every queue/schedule function fail to deploy while the Firestore triggers
# succeed (#1108). The preflight refuses that up front.
FUNCTIONS_REGION=

# Firestore database id. ⚠️ This repo's database is literally named `default`,
# NOT `(default)` — a trigger bound to the unnamed database deploys cleanly and
# then never fires. Inlined by the mercado-livre and whatsapp builds only.
FIREBASE_DATABASE_ID=

# The mercado-livre queue/schedule region — the one `*_TASKS_REGION` that IS
# inlined (its build.mjs `define`s it; the other channels' are runtime reads).
# ⚠️ Must ALSO be set on the App Hosting backend
# (apps/mercado-livre/apphosting.yaml) — the backend is what enqueues, and a
# mismatch makes the Admin SDK resolve us-central1 and drop the task silently.
MERCADO_LIVRE_TASKS_REGION=
